  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-01-05T23:15:16.515Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Today, while you could have an avatar that ranks excellent, if it's bounds size exceed the ranking limit, it will be marked \"very poor\" - however this doesn't actually matter, because bounds size doesn't prevent a model from being displayed. The suggestion is to either make bounds size cause a fallback (or shrink the model to the next size) or remove the bounds size as a requirement altogether.\n\nI'm personally of the opinion that models that are insanely massive should be limited by the ranking system, so not just anybody can block your view with a huge model at any time.",
